# What does not belong in the build context.
#
# target/ is 3.7 GB of build output. It was being copied into every image, which made a
# deploy take ~7 minutes and, worse, baked a stale binary into the image that only the
# entrypoint's "sources newer than binary" check could catch. The container mounts the
# project directory at runtime anyway, so the compiler output it uses is the host's — the
# copy in the image was pure cost.
target/
data/
.git/
.gitignore
tmp/
*.log
*.tmp
node_modules/
